# Server-side / operational scripts that are not browser assets.
#
# vercel.json's "*.js" build glob was publishing these, so
# https://www.bearpark.xyz/server.js served the full 394KB backend source.
# The 404 route in vercel.json stops new requests, but Cloudflare and Vercel
# both still held a cached 200 and kept revalidating it against the file that
# was still present in the deployment. Removing them from the upload means
# there is nothing left to revalidate against.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS REQUIRED. .vercelignore uses .gitignore syntax, where a bare
# "server.js" matches at EVERY level -- it would also exclude backend/server.js,
# which is the file vercel.json actually builds and `npm start` runs.
#
# Root server.js is only referenced by the local "dev" script (node server.js).
/server.js
/daily-airdrop-snapshot.js
/reset-specific-wallet.js
